   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "f is a product of x and the composite ln(cos(x^2)), so f'(x) = ln(cos(x^2)) + x d/dx[ln(cos(x^2))].",
         "mathjson": [
            "Ln",
            [
               "Cos",
               [
                  "Power",
                  "x",
                  2
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The composite has three layers: the log gives 1/cos(x^2), the cosine gives -sin(x^2), and x^2 gives 2x. Their product is -2x tan(x^2).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            -2,
            "x",
            [
               "Tan",
               [
                  "Power",
                  "x",
                  2
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute into the product rule: f'(x) = ln(cos(x^2)) - 2x^2 tan(x^2).",
